From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] pastix.c: accept a stalled refinement with a small residual

PaStiX factorizes with static pivoting (small pivots are perturbed, not
exchanged). For RVEs with beam fibers and *EQUATION constraints the
factorization can be a mediocre preconditioner: GMRES then stalls slightly
above ccx's hard 1e-12 target (observed: 2.4e-11 after 50 iterations, on a
fresh double-precision factorization) and ccx exited with status 5 after also
retrying without diagonal scaling.

Accept such a solution when the relative residual reported by PaStiX
(DPARM_RELATIVE_ERROR) is below 1e-9 -- still orders of magnitude tighter than
the Newton tolerance -- and print a note.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/ccx_2.23/src/pastix.c
+++ b/ccx_2.23/src/pastix.c
@@ -916,6 +916,16 @@
 	SFREE(b);
     b = NULL;
 
+    // GMRES can stall just above its 1e-12 target when the (statically pivoted)
+    // factorization is a poor preconditioner; such a solution is still far more
+    // accurate than ccx's Newton tolerance, so accept it below 1e-9
+    if( rc == -1 && pdparm[DPARM_RELATIVE_ERROR] >= 0. &&
+        pdparm[DPARM_RELATIVE_ERROR] < 1e-9 ){
+        printf("PaStiX: refinement stalled at relative residual %e, solution accepted\n",
+               pdparm[DPARM_RELATIVE_ERROR]);
+        rc = 0;
+    }
+
     modePrev = mode;
     if( !rc ) firstIter = 0;
     if( rc == -1 && globDoublePrecision && !noScale ){
